Local KeePassXC 2.8.0 changes for fingerprint Quick Unlock on this machine.

1. DatabaseOpenWidget::enterKey: a command-line (--pw-stdin) or D-Bus unlock
   stores Quick Unlock credentials like a typed one. Upstream skips that for
   passwords not typed into the window; keepassxc-autounlock.nix unlocks at
   login that way, so without this every later unlock asked for the master
   password.
2. Quick Unlock without a window: raising the main window (tray click,
   starting keepassxc again) or a request through the unlock dialog (browser
   extension, Auto-Type) while locked runs the fingerprint prompt first with
   the window hidden; the window/dialog appears only if that fails or is
   cancelled. Upstream always shows the window and then the prompt.
3. Polkit::getKey: wait for the prompt's answer without blocking the GUI
   (excluding user input), one prompt at a time, with a 5-minute D-Bus
   timeout. Upstream blocks the GUI, so Hyprland offered to kill a "hung"
   KeePassXC, and gave up on answers slower than D-Bus's default 25 s.

